**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** A relabelled item moves to the file of its new label (001 §A: an item is `<label>.item-json`; step 218: no member renamed an item until this section; the S7.2 brief: label edits, writes through KitProxy). In `OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs`, on step 219's `type KitLibraryContext with` extension, documented in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2: `member this.recordRelabelledItem (previous : Item) (relabelled : Item) : Result<unit, KitLibraryError>`, where `relabelled` is `previous` under a new label (`relabelledAmong`, step 236). When the two labels' `fileStem`s differ ignoring case, it records `relabelled` through `this.recordItem` (step 219) and then deletes the old file through `this.kit.proxy.deleteKindFile ItemKitFile previous.label.fileStem` (step 127); when that delete fails, it deletes the new file through the same verb, logs that delete's own failure with `Logger.logError` carrying its `describe`, and answers the first error as `KitLibraryKitErr`, so a failed relabel leaves the item under its old label and never two files of one `ItemId`, which `readItems` refuses (step 218). When the stems are equal ignoring case (`lp1` to `LP1`), the kit root being one Windows folder, it deletes the old file first and then records `relabelled`; when that record fails it writes `previous` back through `this.kit.proxy.writeItem` (step 218), logging that write's own failure, and answers the first error. Under a read-only kit the first write or delete answers `KitReadOnlyErr` and nothing is written. No other member is added. Tests, in `KitLibraryTests` (steps 139, 219), over its Built-in library and its in-memory kit opened read-write, with a CPL1 item made by step 216's `ItemDraft` over `LibraryModelChoice (BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId)` and `DialMounted DialPositive` recorded through `recordItem`: `a relabelled item moves to the file of its new label`: relabelled `CPL 1` and recorded through `recordRelabelledItem`, `paths` holds `CPL 1.item-json` and no `CPL1.item-json`, and `kit.proxy.readItems ()` answers the item under its new label and its id. `a relabel that changes only the case rewrites the one file`: an item recorded as `cpl1` and relabelled `CPL1` leaves exactly one item file, `CPL1.item-json`, and `readItems` answers the item labelled `CPL1`. `a relabel whose old file cannot be deleted leaves the item under its old label`: over a context whose proxy is a record update of the in-memory one refusing `deleteKindFile` of the stem `CPL1` with `KitIoErr`, relabelling CPL1 `CPL 1` answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitIoErr _)`, and `readItems` answers CPL1 alone under its old label.

**Acceptance.** After the relabel lands, `KitLibraryContext.recordRelabelledItem` MUST leave the item in the file of its new label alone, rewrite one file for a change of case, and leave the item under its old label when the old file cannot be deleted; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a relabelled item moves to the file of its new label`, `a relabel that changes only the case rewrites the one file` and `a relabel whose old file cannot be deleted leaves the item under its old label`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the fourteen s24 invariants MUST pass.
